  "summary": "Fractions as parts of wholes, area models, proper, improper, and mixed fractions, ancient Indian algorithms for fraction operations (Brahmagupta's methods), and comparing fractions.",
  "theory_summary": [
    {
      "topic": "Fraction Representation & Area Models",
      "content": "A fraction $\\frac{a}{b}$ represents $a$ equal parts out of a total of $b$ parts of a whole."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Brahmagupta's Fraction Algorithms",
      "content": "In the *Brāhmasphuṭasiddhānta* (628 CE), Brahmagupta codified:\n- Addition/Subtraction: $\\frac{a}{b} \\pm \\frac{c}{d} = \\frac{ad \\pm bc}{bd}$.\n- Multiplication: $\\frac{a}{b} \\times \\frac{c}{d} = \\frac{ac}{bd}$."
    }
  ],
